  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026, done under RBC-PHARM-07. All 7 patients reviewed. Each one has a signed progress note giving the values used, the rule result and the cited records.\n\n- Irene Castellano (pt-0061): apixaban raised from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily. She meets none of the dose criteria (age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02). The outside infectious disease letter of 9/10 says her itraconazole course ended 8/14.\n- Frank Delgado (pt-0003): stays on rivaroxaban 20 mg daily (net no change). I first lowered him to 15 mg based on a St. Brigid creatinine of 160 µmol/L (CrCl 44). St. Brigid then sent a corrected result of 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault. That gives CrCl 59.9, so I put him back on 20 mg and noted why.\n- Raymond Duquette (pt-0041): apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily because of his active itraconazole order (started 10/6). He meets no other criteria. The itraconazole order was not touched.\n- Norman Fairweather (pt-0062): no change; 5 mg twice daily is correct. Two St. Brigid ED creatinines came in during the review: 1.70 mg/dL on 10/21, then 1.13 mg/dL on 10/22. Using the latest, he meets only the age criterion (82).\n- Eugene Moravec (pt-0038): rivaroxaban raised from 15 to 20 mg daily. With his actual weight (96 kg) and SCr 1.45, CrCl is 56. The May pharmacist note had used ideal body weight. During the review he sent a portal message reporting 185 lb on his home scale. The policy doesn't count a reported weight, so the decision stands. If a clinic weight confirms about 84 kg or less, CrCl would be about 50 or lower and he would need 15 mg, so he should be weighed at his next visit.\n- Marjorie Pellegrino (pt-0043): rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to 15 mg daily. A new creatinine of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) came in as the review started. With 71 kg, age 75 and the female factor, CrCl is 43.6.\n- Harold Vance (pt-0002): stays on apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily (net no change), but now for a different reason. His weight (64.9 kg) and SCr (1.21) have recovered, leaving only the age criterion, so I first raised him to 5 mg. A St. Brigid dermatology letter dated 10/22 then arrived saying they started itraconazole that day for 12 weeks. That interaction calls for 2.5 mg, so I set it back and noted why.\n\nFollow-up:\n- Duquette and Vance should have their apixaban dose re-checked when their itraconazole courses end (Vance around 1/14/2027).\n\nI closed the 5 inbox items that arrived during the review, each linked to its note or order. Your older inbox items not related to this review are still open.",
